{%- comment -%}
  Floating "Shop now" button, bottom right of every page.

  It takes the corner the WhatsApp button used, and only while that button
  is hidden. The two share one spot: turning WhatsApp back on hands the
  corner back, rather than stacking a second button on top of it. Like
  WhatsApp, it stays put while the page scrolls. The only thing that moves
  it is the sticky Add to bag bar.

  It sits below the cart drawer, mobile nav and age gate in the stacking
  order (see the z-index scale in base.css), so it never floats over a
  panel the visitor has opened or over the age gate.

  Not on the cart page: the button sits exactly where the full-width
  checkout button ends up while scrolling, and nothing should compete
  with checkout for that tap.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign wa_phone = settings.whatsapp_phone | strip
  assign whatsapp_showing = false
  if settings.whatsapp_enabled and wa_phone != blank and template.name != 'cart'
    assign whatsapp_showing = true
  endif

  assign shop_href = '/products/dunrobin-gin'
  assign shop_product = all_products['dunrobin-gin']
  if shop_product != empty and shop_product.url != blank
    assign shop_href = shop_product.url
  endif
-%}

{%- unless template.name == 'cart' or whatsapp_showing -%}
  <a class="button shop-now-float" href="{{ shop_href }}">
    {% render 'icon', name: 'shopping-cart' %}
    {{ 'general.shop_now.label' | t }}
  </a>
{%- endunless -%}
